    "content": "Bobby Hurley is the older brother of UConn men’s basketball coach Dan Hurley. A legendary Duke All-American point guard and former NBA player, Bobby is currently a head coach (formerly at Arizona State). They are the sons of Hall of Fame New Jersey high school coach Bob Hurley Sr.. Key Details About Bobby Hurley: Playing Career: Bobby was a standout player at Duke University, winning two NCAA championships (1991,1992). He is the NCAA all-time assist leader and was the 7th pick in the 1993 NBA Draft. Coaching Career: Following his playing career, he became a college coach, notably leading the Arizona State Sun Devils. Family Background: Both Danny and Bobby were coached by their father, Bob Hurley Sr., at St. Anthony High School in Jersey City. Brotherly Bond: Despite competing as coaches, the brothers are very close, with Dan often citing Bobby as a mentor, notes NCAA.com.",
